  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"y equals 4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y equals x squared minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"y equals 4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, substituting <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in the second equation of the given system yields <math alttext=\"4 x equals x squared minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"0 equals x squared minus 4 x minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 2 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. By the zero product property, <math alttext=\"x minus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> or <math alttext=\"x plus 2 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x minus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 2 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, solutions to the given system of equations occur when <math alttext=\"x equals 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and when <math alttext=\"x equals negative 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a solution to the given system of equations is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math alttext=\"x greater than 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Since <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> is greater than <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, it follows that the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>.</p>",
